reflect on on some of the things we might well have missed out on because of the way we've been parented or the way that you've been treated in relationships by past or present partners and you know when you develop that insight and when I've been working with clients who've developed that insight that maybe their experiences haven't been the same as other people there really can be that really powerful grief reaction for what you've missed out on. So grief, as you might well know, is not always linked to, you know, the death or dying of someone or something. It can be what you've missed out on. And we saw this first begin to be spoken about publicly around the
反思那些我们可能因为成长环境或过去及现在伴侣对待我们的方式而错失的东西。你知道，当你产生这种洞察力时——我曾与那些产生这种洞察力的客户合作过——意识到他们的经历可能与其他人不同，那种因为错失而产生的悲伤反应是非常强烈的。所以，正如你可能知道的那样，悲伤并不总是与某人或某事的死亡或离世有关。它也可以是因为你错失了某些东西。我们第一次看到这种观点被公开讨论是在……

